  "details": "Currently, the Avatar Ranking System, as far as most are aware, is targeted, on mobile, towards what is deemed as \"performant\" on Quest 1 hardware.\n\n**However**, Quest 2 hardware, in many ways, excels beyond that of first generation equipment. — In many ways, avatars on Quest ranked \"very poor\", *but with stats equivalent to \"Medium\" or \"Good\" on PC*, run well on the system, **with no noticeable performance decrease compared to their higher-ranked siblings**.\n\nAs such, whilst it would be good to *maintain shared* ***limitations*** *in regards to avatar components*, between Quest 1 and Quest 2, the *rankings provided to avatars should be adjusted when displayed on Quest 2 hardware*.\nNot only would this allow avatars to have a fairer ranking, when displayed to Quest 2 users, but it would allow Quest 2 content developers to utilize more SDK3 features (props, interchangeable clothes, materials) without being penalized by the ranking system for reasonable mesh-renderer counts, material slots, and/or reasonable poly-counts above the current 20K limit.\n\nIn practice, the VRCSDK would remain mostly unchanged, providing the Quest 1 avatar ranking. However, based on the avatar's stats, a Quest 2 ranking would also be assigned.\n\nThe VRC mobile client would then identify the hardware generation being ran on (Quest 1, Quest 2), and use the ranking relevant to its hardware.",
